From 4d9a7e771e2b9ff9b637c4ba94ed74bfd0d35721 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicole Muzzin <nicole@muzz.in>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 16:30:41 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] grid: keep one sparse auto-placement cursor per row in step 2

Step 2 of the placement algorithm places an item with a definite row "past
any grid items previously placed in this row by this step". The lookup
used the last auto-placed cell in the row, which also counts cells covered
by an item placed in an earlier row that spans into this one. With
`grid-area: 1 / span 2` followed by `1 / span 2 / span 2` and `2 / span 2`
in four columns, the third item skipped past the second item's cells in
row 2 and was pushed into new implicit columns, where Chrome puts it under
the first item. Track a cursor per row start line instead, as Blink does.
The cell-occupancy lookups this replaces have no other users.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
